Z||000008||Smoooooth GT||06-12-2001||11:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>are you still doing the fiberglass bondo thing on the facias too? any flex/cracking problems? any extra prep work for good bonding? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well...  alot more glass then bondo here... 97% vs. 3%.  No problem with cracking so far, I'm using xtra flex agent on the fascia's!!!                Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka..FieroSEt <BR>cell.. 903 445 0849  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new_sig.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Smoooooth GT||06-13-2001||12:08 AM||||Thank's EVERYBODY for the nice comment's.<BR>As far as the exhaust goes... The plan TODAY is for me routing the Flowmaster out just in front of the rear tires. But ...  I have the option NOW to... route the exhaust outta the middle rear...  Then we come to the silly , small, other problem...  That dang license plate. Well....  I'm sad to say that I'm going to CUT Ferrari-Momo's 1st Generation Euro Light's... and glass in a license plate holder in the middle of the car between the Vette light's. I think that will look good. <BR>I think that I'm going to sell the 3" wing extention's that I bought from Outlaw Performance for this project.  <BR>All idea's welcome...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka..FieroSEt <BR>cell.. 903 445 0849  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new_sig.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||06-13-2001||12:13 AM||||What did you use to fill in the gap where you removed the trim (on the sides)?  How did you fasten the body panels to the frame?  And, how can you remove the panels in case (God forbid) of an accident?<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000011||Smoooooth GT||06-13-2001||12:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>What did you use to fill in the gap where you removed the trim (on the sides)?  How did you fasten the body panels to the frame?  And, how can you remove the panels in case (God forbid) of an accident?<P>MM</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>MM...  I'm glad to finally get a reply from one of the many Fiero God's...<BR>I fastened the panel's to the body in all the places that I could with sheet metal screw's...  Then filled the slot's(under trim) with Bondo with flex mix, Then glassed over them several times over...  I then have used filler to do a little filling over the glassed area's..I have slammed the door pretty hard several times with no after effect so far. As far as REMOVING a panel... forget it.. But I figure if I'm in a accident, the panel and glassing replacment will be ness anyhow... Thank's Monkeyman for your reply. all idea's welcome!!!  Steve||||reg||1
Z||000012||ferrari_momo||06-13-2001||12:37 AM||||ummm.. if u were gonna put the exhaust through the middle. you will need MoMo's new trunk cover!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  it is being developed for my 308 cars' trunks.  oh yea, i got the stuff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  hmm... i like the bumper!  very nice.  gee, i will have to make 355 rear bumper to go with my euro tail light kit now.  but keep up the good work buddy.  meet you one day in person.  i better not park my euro-fiero next to yours.  hehehe<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||11
